+Exit gate: This is a central novelty gate. Compare every result with existing hull papers. 
+Phase 5 — Gray maps 
+Objective: Construct a suitable map to a finite-field alphabet and determine its exact algebraic and metric properties. 
+Required deliverables: Map definition; proof of additivity/linearity as applicable; weight results; dual/hull relationship 
+theorem or explicit non-preservation result. 
+Exit gate: Do not assume Gray maps preserve duals or hulls. 
+Phase 6 — Quantum constructions 
+Objective: Select a valid quantum construction (CSS or another justified route) and prove all inclusion/orthogonality and 
