+# Phase 3 — Stage 3B: Enumeration of Galois hull dimensions
+
+**Title of the programme (unchanged):** *Codes over the matrix ring $R=M_2(A_t)$,
+$A_t=\mathbb F_q[u]/\langle u^t\rangle$: structure, duality and enumeration.*
+
+**Script:** `04_COMPUTATION/phase3_stage3b_hull_enumeration.py`
+**Log:** `04_COMPUTATION/phase3_stage3b_hull_log.txt`
+(696 lines, **206 checks, 206 PASS, 0 FAIL**, seed $20261109$, Python 3.11.2,
+two consecutive runs **byte-identical**, log SHA-256 `c8904a23…59814`).
+
+---
+
+## 0. Scope, conventions, and what is carried in
+
+### 0.1 Standing conventions (unchanged)
+
+* $A_t=\mathbb F_q[u]/\langle u^t\rangle$, $R=M_2(A_t)$, $R_n=R[X]/\langle X^n-1\rangle$,
+  $B=A_t[X]/\langle X^n-1\rangle$, so $R_n\cong M_2(B)$.
+* **Codes are right ideals of $R_n$.** By Morita (Stage 2A, T-077) a right ideal is
+  $I_W=\{M\in M_2(B): \text{columns of } M \text{ lie in } W\}$ for a unique
+  $B$-submodule $W\le B^2$; $I_W=hR_n$ is principal $\iff$ $W=\operatorname{im}h$ is
+  generated by $\le 2$ elements over $B$ $\iff$ $\mu_B(W)\le 2$.
+* $\theta_s$ = (Frobenius $\sigma_s$ on entries) $\circ$ (transpose), $\operatorname{rev}$ is
+  $X\mapsto X^{-1}$, and
+  $C^{\perp_s}=\operatorname{rev}(\operatorname{ann}_r(\theta_s(C)))$
+  (Stage 2C Thm 3.8); $\operatorname{Hull}_s(C)=C\cap C^{\perp_s}$.
+* $\mu_B(W)$ = minimal number of $B$-generators of $W$ (Nakayama lift, Stage 2C).
+
+### 0.2 Imported results (used, not re-proved)
+
+| ID | statement |
+|---|---|
+| T-077 (Stage 2A) | $W(hR_n)=\operatorname{im}h$; $I_W\leftrightarrow W$ is a bijection |
+| Stage 2C Thm 3.8 | $C^{\perp_s}=\operatorname{rev}(\operatorname{ann}_r(\theta_s(C)))$ |
+| Stage 3A Thm 2.2 | $W(C^{\perp_s})=\bigcap_i\ker\theta_s(\operatorname{rev}g_i)$ |
+| **Stage 3A Thm 3.3** | $\operatorname{Hull}_s(C)=I_{W\cap W'}$, $\dim\operatorname{Hull}_s(C)=2\dim_{\mathbb F_q}(W\cap W')$ |
+| **Stage 3A Thm 3.5** | in the split regime $(C^{\perp_s})_j=(C_{\tau(j)})^{\perp_s}$, $\tau=\pi^{-1}\circ\rho$ characterised by $\zeta_{\tau(j)}^{p^s}=\zeta_j^{-1}$; $\dim\operatorname{Hull}_s(C)=\sum_j\dim\big(C_j\cap (C_{\tau(j)})^{\perp_s}\big)$; $\tau=\mathrm{id}\iff n\mid p^s+1$ |
+| T-102 (Stage 2B) | over a chain ring every submodule of $B^2$ is $\le 2$-generated |
+
+### 0.3 What Stage 3B does **not** claim
+
+* **No Gray map** (Phase 5), **no CSS/EAQECC construction** (Phase 6), **no quantum
+  parameters**, **no manuscript text**. Those stages are not started.
+* No **universal closed form** for $\dim\operatorname{Hull}_s(C)$; no closed form at all
+  outside the split regime (§6.4).
+* Hull enumerators are **not** used to infer anything about quantum codes.
+* Nothing below is sampled-and-called-exhaustive: every `[EXH]` line is exhaustive over
+  the family named in the line, every `[SMP]` line states the sample size.
+
+### 0.4 The eight parameter sets and the three regimes
+
+| $(q,t,n)$ | regime | $\lvert B\rvert$ | $\dim_{\mathbb F_q}R_n$ | enumeration |
