+## 1. Task A — the four counting problems
+
+Four **different** numbers are attached to the same ring. They are never mixed, and none
+is derived from another.
+
+1. **distinct right ideals of $R_n$** $=$ distinct $B$-submodules $W\le B^2$;
+2. **distinct generator matrices** $=$ ordered $k$-tuples of elements of $W$ that generate
+   $W$ as a $B$-module (counted per module; the total over all modules is $\lvert B^2\rvert^k$);
+3. **unit-equivalence classes** $=$ orbits of $R_n^\times=\mathrm{GL}_2(B)$ acting on right
+   ideals by **left** multiplication, i.e. $W\mapsto UW$ under Morita;
+4. **Morita-equivalent submodules** $=$ isomorphism classes of the $B$-modules $W$.
+
+Two remarks that decide the definitions:
+
+* **(3) must be left multiplication.** Right multiplication is *trivial*: $I\cdot u=I$ for
+  every unit $u$ and every right ideal $I$. The "scalar" variant $W\mapsto uW$ for
+  $u\in B^\times$ is *also* trivial, because $W$ is a $B$-module, so $uW=W$; the log says
+  this explicitly on every case so that the trap is documented rather than silently avoided.
+  Left multiplication by $U\in\mathrm{GL}_2(B)$ is the non-trivial action, and under
+  Morita $U\,I_W=I_{UW}$.
+* **(4) uses a complete invariant where one exists.** In the chain regime $B$ is a chain
+  ring and the valuation/SNF type $\bigl(\text{parts }a_i\bigr)$, recovered from
