+## 6. Task F — a closed form in the split regime (τ-orbit transfer matrix)
+
+### 6.1 Statement
+
+> **Theorem T-169 (hull enumerator, split regime).** Assume the split regime
+> $B\cong\prod_{j=0}^{n-1}A_t$, let $L=L(A_t^2)$ be the (finite) lattice of $A_t$-submodules
+> of $A_t^2$, let $\delta_s(V)$ be the local Galois dual ($=W(C_V^{\perp_s})$ for the
+> $n=1$ instance), and let $\tau$ be the Stage-3A permutation of the components. Define
+> the $|L|\times|L|$ matrix over $\mathbb Z[Z]$ (resp. $\mathbb Z[U,Z]$)
+> $$N[V,W]=Z^{\,\dim_{\mathbb F_q}\left(V\,\cap\,\delta_s(W)\right)},\qquad
+>   N_U[V,W]=U^{\,2\dim_{\mathbb F_q}V}\,Z^{\,\dim_{\mathbb F_q}\left(V\,\cap\,\delta_s(W)\right)} .$$
+> Then, summing over all codes,
+> $$H_{q,t,n,s}(Z)\;=\;\prod_{\tau\text{-orbits }O}\ \operatorname{Tr}\!\bigl(N^{\,|O|}\bigr),
+> \qquad
+> E_{q,t,n,s}(U,Z)\;=\;\prod_{\tau\text{-orbits }O}\ \operatorname{Tr}\!\bigl(N_U^{\,|O|}\bigr).$$
+
+*Proof.* By Morita and CRT, a code is exactly a tuple $(V_0,\dots,V_{n-1})\in L^n$, and by
+Stage 3A Thm 3.5
+$\dim\operatorname{Hull}_s(C)=\sum_j\dim_{\mathbb F_q}\bigl(V_j\cap\delta_s(V_{\tau(j)})\bigr)$
+(the $n=1$ dual is the same $\delta_s$ in every component, the component ring being
+$A_t$). Group the coordinates by $\tau$-orbits. For one orbit
+$j_1\to j_2\to\cdots\to j_\ell\to j_1$ the sum over the tuples indexed by that orbit of
+$\prod_i N[V_{j_i},V_{j_{i+1}}]$ (indices mod $\ell$) is exactly the expansion of
+$\operatorname{Tr}(N^\ell)=\sum_{i_1,\dots,i_\ell}N[i_1,i_2]N[i_2,i_3]\cdots N[i_\ell,i_1]$,
+and the exponent adds up to the orbit's contribution to $\dim\operatorname{Hull}_s(C)$.
+Distinct orbits involve disjoint coordinate sets, so summing over $L^n$ factorises into
+the product over orbits. The bivariate version is identical with the extra factor
+$U^{\sum_j2\dim V_j}=U^{\dim C}$. ∎
+
+The proof uses **only** (i) the Morita/CRT description of codes, (ii) Stage 3A Thm 3.5,
+and (iii) the definition of a matrix trace. It is not a data fit: the states ($L$), the
+transitions ($V\cap\delta_s(W)$), the initialisation, and the exactly-once counting are
+all given by the theorem, and there are no inadmissible tuples because **every** tuple in
+$L^n$ is a code.
+
+### 6.2 Tested range (exhaustive)
+
+| $(q,t,n)$ | $s$ | $\tau$ (as a list) | orbits | $H(Z)$ from $\prod_O\operatorname{Tr}(N^{|O|})$ vs brute force over all codes |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| $(4,1,3)$ | 0 | $[0,2,1]$ | $\{0\},\{1,2\}$ | identical (343 codes) |
+| $(4,1,3)$ | 1 | $[0,1,2]$ (id) | three singletons | identical |
+| $(9,1,2)$ | 0 | $[0,1]$ (id) | two singletons | identical (144 codes) |
+| $(9,1,2)$ | 1 | $[0,1]$ (id) | two singletons | identical |
+| $(4,2,3)$ | 0 | $[0,2,1]$ | $\{0\},\{1,2\}$ | identical (35 937 codes) |
+| $(4,2,3)$ | 1 | $[0,1,2]$ (id) | three singletons | identical |
+
+Both the univariate and the bivariate identity are checked (`[EXH]`) in every row, and
+$\tau$ is computed independently from the characterisation $\zeta_{\tau(j)}^{p^s}=\zeta_j^{-1}$
+(equivalently $\tau(j)\equiv-j\,(p^s)^{-1}\bmod n$), agreeing with Stage 3A's table.
+Consistently with Stage 3A Thm 3.5, $\tau=\mathrm{id}\iff n\mid p^s+1$, which the log
+prints for every case.
+
+### 6.3 Why the factor 2 is in the exponent
+
+The local entry is $\dim_{\mathbb F_q}(V\cap\delta_s(W))$ but the hull contributes
+$2\dim_{\mathbb F_q}$ of it (Stage 3A Thm 3.3). Omitting the factor $2$ produced
+enumerators with the **right coefficients and half the exponents** — the bug was caught
+by the brute-force comparison and is recorded here because the failure mode is
+instructive: matching coefficients are not evidence for a formula.
+
+### 6.4 Limitations
+
+* The formula is **proved only in the split regime** (it needs a CRT decomposition into
+  $n$ components on which $\tau$ acts). It is *tested* on $(4,1,3),(9,1,2),(4,2,3)$.
+* In the **chain** regime there is one component and the statement degenerates to
+  $H=\operatorname{Tr}(N)$ with $N$ a $1\times1$-index matrix — true but vacuous; the log
+  says so instead of printing a tautological pass.
+* In the **wild** regime no component decomposition exists; no transfer matrix is defined
+  and none is claimed (**O-3.4**).
