+## 3. Task C — exact quantum distance certification
+
+Twenty-two codes are certified: the three strongest of each route, plus the
+strongest code of each family.  **No code is re-selected by invariants** — the
+search stores the image basis of every reported code, so the certified code is
+literally the code that produced the reported parameters.  Three methods are
+run on each:
+
+* **M1** — complete enumeration of the classical quotient (every codeword of
+  `G` outside `E`); exact and complete whenever `q^{dim G} ≤ 2·10^6`.
+* **M2** — an independent algorithm: an increasing-weight support search, which
+  for each support solves a left-kernel problem instead of enumerating.
+* **M3** — an exhaustive search of the **ambient quantum space** `F_q^{2N}` in
+  increasing *symplectic* weight, testing `v ∈ V^{⊥_ω}` (commutes with the
+  whole group) and `v ∉ V` (acts non-trivially).  M3 is the only method that
+  works at the level of the quantum error group itself; it is complete only up
+  to the weight it reaches, and a return of "none" is reported as the proved
+  lower bound `d > w`.
