+| **T-144** | **B — the principal hull formula.** For $C=gR_n$: $\mathrm{Hull}_s(C)=gR_n\cap\operatorname{rev}(\operatorname{ann}_r(\theta_s(g)))=gR_n\cap\operatorname{ann}_r(\theta_s(\operatorname{rev}g))=I_W$ with $W=\operatorname{im}g\cap\ker\theta_s(\operatorname{rev}g)$, and $\lvert\mathrm{Hull}\rvert=\lvert W\rvert^2$, $\dim\mathrm{Hull}=2\dim W$. Both inclusions are by the definition of intersection. Roles: $\operatorname{rev}$ is an automorphism (hence movable into $\theta_s$) and is the identity iff $n\le2$; the annihilator is the **right** one of the element $\theta_s(g)$, not $\operatorname{ann}_l$ and not the annihilator of the ideal; $\theta_s$ turns the right ideal into a left one, which is why one generator suffices | — | Stage 3A Thm 2.1 | T-077, T-125 | **`PROVED IN PHASE 3 STAGE 3A`** | 3 independent routes (definition / annihilator / Morita) agree on 40 codes per pair; elementwise inclusions enumerated on 6 codes at 13/17 pairs | §2.1 |
