+
+####################################################################################################
+  TASK A -- the four counting problems, separately for each parameter set
+####################################################################################################
+  (1) distinct right ideals of R_n = distinct B-submodules of B^2
+  (2) distinct generator matrices  = generating tuples of the submodule
+  (3) unit-equivalence classes     = orbits of R_n^x = GL_2(B) acting by
+                                     LEFT multiplication on right ideals
+                                     (i.e. W -> U W under Morita)
+  (4) Morita-equivalent submodules = isomorphism classes of the B-modules
+  These four numbers are NEVER mixed: (1) != (2) != (3) != (4) in general.
+
+---- counting problems for (q,t,n)=(4,1,1) ---------------------------------------------------------
+  (1) distinct right ideals of R_n = distinct B-submodules of B^2 : 7
+  [EXH] (4,1,1): the numbers of generating 1-tuples sum to |B^2|^1   PASS  16 vs 16
+      per-module counts range 0..3 ; #modules with a generating 1-tuple: 6
+      #cyclic (1-generated) modules: 6
+  [EXH] (4,1,1): the numbers of generating 2-tuples sum to |B^2|^2   PASS  256 vs 256
+      per-module counts range 1..180 ; #modules with a generating 2-tuple: 7
+      #cyclic (1-generated) modules: 6
+  (3) #unit-equivalence classes (orbits of R_n^x = GL_2(B) acting by LEFT multiplication; 10 generators, |B^x| = 3) : 3
+  [EXH] (4,1,1): the reduced generating set of GL_2(B) gives the same orbit count as the full one PASS  3 vs 3
+      NB the 'scalar' action u*W (u in B^x) is TRIVIAL: W is a B-module, so uW = W for every unit u
+  (4) #Morita-equivalence classes (isomorphism classes of the B-modules W) : 3
+  [EXH] (4,1,1): the type invariant separates the lattice at least as finely as the dimension PASS  3 >= 3
+  [EXH] (4,1,1): #unit-equivalence classes >= #Morita classes (unit equivalence implies B-module isomorphism) PASS  3 >= 3
+  NB: 7 (right ideals), 3 (unit classes), 3 (Morita classes) are three DIFFERENT counting problems; none is derived from another.
+
+---- counting problems for (q,t,n)=(4,1,2) ---------------------------------------------------------
+  (1) distinct right ideals of R_n = distinct B-submodules of B^2 : 33
