+PART C.  TASK C: the map from the Gray image to physical qudit coordinates
+==============================================================================
+
+C1.  how many physical coordinates?
+-----------------------------------
+  The Gray map phi_n : R^n -> F_q^{N} is an F_q-linear bijection with
+  N = dim_{F_q} R^n = (dim_{F_q} R) * n = 4tn  (dim R = 4t).
+  One qudit of dimension q carries one F_q coordinate, so
+      N_phys = N = 4tn,
+  DERIVED from dim_{F_q} R = 4 * dim_{F_q} A_t = 4t, not assumed.
+  [EXH] C1  (q,t,n)=(4,1,2): N_phys = 4tn = 8 (= dim_{F_q} R^n)      PASS  [EXH] dim_{F_q} A_t = 1, dim_{F_q} R = 4
+  [EXH] C1  (q,t,n)=(4,2,1): N_phys = 4tn = 8 (= dim_{F_q} R^n)      PASS  [EXH] dim_{F_q} A_t = 2, dim_{F_q} R = 8
+  [EXH] C1  (q,t,n)=(4,2,2): N_phys = 4tn = 16 (= dim_{F_q} R^n)     PASS  [EXH] dim_{F_q} A_t = 2, dim_{F_q} R = 8
+  [EXH] C1  (q,t,n)=(4,2,3): N_phys = 4tn = 24 (= dim_{F_q} R^n)     PASS  [EXH] dim_{F_q} A_t = 2, dim_{F_q} R = 8
+
+C2.  converting the Hankel form: Psi(u) = u * TT, TT = I_{4n} (x) T
+-------------------------------------------------------------------
+  With sigma_s = id the transported form is the bilinear form with
+  matrix J = I_{4n} (x) H_t.  Since J^2 = I, a block T with
+  T^T H_t T = I_t gives (u TT).(v TT) = u TT TT^T v^T = u J^{-1} v^T
+  = u J v^T = <u,v>, i.e. Psi turns the transported form into the
+  Euclidean form.  Eight properties are checked for each case.
+  (q,t,n,s)=(4,1,2,0) N=8 : congruence T with T^T H_t T = I_t : True
+    (1) T^T H_t T = I_t            : True
+    (2) TT TT^T = J                : True
+    (3) J^2 = I                    : True
+    (4) TT invertible              : True
+    (5) TT monomial                : True   (monomial <=> Hamming weights preserved)
+    (6) (u TT).(v TT) = u J v^T    : True
+    (7) TT commutes with the shift : True
+    (8) Psi is F_q-linear          : True
+  [EXH] C2  (q,t,n)=(4,1,2): the eight properties of the physical-coordinate map Psi PASS  [EXH] monomial=True, shift-commuting=True
+  (q,t,n,s)=(9,2,1,0) N=8 : congruence T with T^T H_t T = I_t : True
+    (1) T^T H_t T = I_t            : True
+    (2) TT TT^T = J                : True
+    (3) J^2 = I                    : True
+    (4) TT invertible              : True
+    (5) TT monomial                : False   (monomial <=> Hamming weights preserved)
+    (6) (u TT).(v TT) = u J v^T    : True
+    (7) TT commutes with the shift : True
+    (8) Psi is F_q-linear          : True
+  [EXH] C2  (q,t,n)=(9,2,1): the eight properties of the physical-coordinate map Psi PASS  [EXH] monomial=False, shift-commuting=True
+  (q,t,n,s)=(4,2,1,0) N=8 : congruence T with T^T H_t T = I_t : False
+       no such T exists (exhaustive): for p = 2 and t even the
+       matrix H_t is alternating, so H_t cannot be congruent to I_t.
+       => the Euclidean route R2 is BLOCKED for this parameter set;
+          only the Galois-native route R1 remains available.
+  (q,t,n,s)=(9,2,2,0) N=16 : congruence T with T^T H_t T = I_t : True
+    (1) T^T H_t T = I_t            : True
+    (2) TT TT^T = J                : True
+    (3) J^2 = I                    : True
+    (4) TT invertible              : True
+    (5) TT monomial                : False   (monomial <=> Hamming weights preserved)
+    (6) (u TT).(v TT) = u J v^T    : True
+    (7) TT commutes with the shift : True
+    (8) Psi is F_q-linear          : True
+  [EXH] C2  (q,t,n)=(9,2,2): the eight properties of the physical-coordinate map Psi PASS  [EXH] monomial=False, shift-commuting=True
+
