+% =====================================================================
+\appendix
+\section{Certification table and comparison data}
+\label{app:tables}
+% =====================================================================
+
+\subsection{The certification table}
+
+Table~\ref{tab:cert} is the complete output of the certification stage: all
+$28$ certified codes, reproduced verbatim from the computation log
+(\filepath{04_COMPUTATION/phase7_extended_search_log.txt}, Part~6). The
+columns M1, M2, M3 record the three independent distance methods of
+Section~\ref{sec:cert}: a dash means the method could not complete, and
+``$>2$'' means the ambient quantum search (M3) reached weight $2$ without
+finding a vector, i.e. it certifies $d\ge3$ as a \emph{lower} bound only.
+The column ``exact'' says yes when all three methods that completed agree
+with the reported value, the stabilizer is $\F_p$-abelian, and $K$ and $c$
+recompute from $k$ and $h_E$.
+
+\begin{table}[ht]
+\centering
+\small
+\caption{All $28$ certified codes (Part~6 of the Phase-7 log, verbatim).
+$S$-def is the entanglement-assisted Singleton defect $N-K+c-2(d-1)$.}
+\label{tab:cert}
+\begin{tabular}{@{}llcrrrrrl@{}}
+\toprule
+code & family & route & $k$ & $K$ & $d$ & $c$
+ & $S$-def & M1 / M2 / M3\\
+\midrule
+$[[24,8,4]]_9$   & $(9,1,6)$ & SO & 8  & 8  & 4  & 0  & 10 & -- / 4 / $>2$\\
+$[[20,4,4]]_4$   & $(4,1,5)$ & SO & 8  & 4  & 4  & 0  & 10 & -- / 4 / $>2$\\
+$[[20,4,4]]_4$   & $(4,1,5)$ & DC & 12 & 4  & 4  & 0  & 10 & -- / 4 / $>2$\\
+$[[20,2,10;18]]_4$ & $(4,1,5)$ & EA & 18 & 2  & 10 & 18 & 18 & 10 / n/a / $>2$\\
