+# Phase 11 / Task C4 — Funding declaration
+
+**Status: RESEARCHER CONFIRMATION REQUIRED. NOTHING HAS BEEN DECLARED.**
+
+## 1. What FFA/Elsevier requires (verified 2026-11-10)
+
+* Authors must disclose **all funding sources** for the work.
+* The **role of the sponsor** must be stated where the sponsor had any
+  involvement in study design; collection, analysis and interpretation of
+  data; writing of the report; or the decision to submit for publication.
+* If the sponsor had **no such involvement**, that must be stated explicitly.
+* If there is **no funding to declare**, Elsevier's standard wording is:
+
+  > This research did not receive any specific grant from funding agencies in
+  > the public, commercial, or not-for-profit sectors.
+
+* Funders are identified by their **full official name**; grant numbers are
+  given where they exist.
+
+## 2. Why this cannot be completed by the agent
+
+Two opposite errors are both available here, and both are serious:
+
+* **Asserting "no funding"** from the mere absence of a grant number in the
+  project files. Absence of evidence is not evidence of absence. Institutional
+  support, a scholarship, a departmental allocation or an in-kind contribution
+  are all funding and none would appear in this repository.
+* **Inventing** a funder, agency or grant number.
+
+The funding status of this work is therefore recorded as **UNCONFIRMED**, and
+the staging copy presents both permitted outcomes without selecting one.
+
+## 3. What the project documentation does and does not show
+
+| source | finding |
+|---|---|
+| Repository content, all phases | **No** grant number, agency name, award number or funding acknowledgement appears in any file. |
+| Manuscript `PAPER/main.tex` | No funding section, no `\thanks` grant, no acknowledgement of support. |
+| Phase 0–8 documentation | Silent on funding. |
+| Inference | **None performed.** |
+
+This is consistent with unfunded work, and also consistent with funded work
+whose support simply was never recorded in the repository. **It does not
+settle the question.**
+
+## 4. Researcher action items
+
+1. State whether the work received any specific grant from a funding agency
+   in the public, commercial, or not-for-profit sectors.
+2. If yes: give the **full official name** of each funder, the **country**,
+   and the **grant number(s)**.
+3. If yes: state the role of the sponsor in study design, data collection and
+   analysis, the decision to publish, or the preparation of the manuscript —
+   or state explicitly that the sponsor had no such involvement.
+4. If no: confirm use of the Elsevier standard sentence above.
+5. Note whether the funder requires a specific acknowledgement wording or an
+   OA mandate.
+6. Confirm whether the APC (USD 3 240, verified 2026-11-10) is to be paid from
+   a grant, an institutional Read & Publish agreement, or otherwise — **if**
+   gold OA is chosen. **Subscription publication carries no charge**, so no
+   funding decision is needed for the subscription route.
+
+**BLOCKING until item 1 is answered.**
