+==============================================================================
+  C1  the Euclidean form on F_q^N is NOT the transported form unless
+      t = 1 and r | s:  J = I_{4n} (x) H_t = I  <=>  t = 1, and the
+      sigma_s-twist is trivial  <=>  r | s.  Measured per family above
+      ('#codes where the EUCLIDEAN orthogonal ... differs').
+  C2  the plain sigma_s-Hermitian form (Gram = I, no Hankel twist) is
+      NOT the transported form unless t = 1 (same counter above).
+  C3  phi_n is NOT a ring-Hamming isometry:  w_H(x) <= wt_Ham(phi_n x)
+      <= 4t w_H(x), and both bounds are attained; the count of words
+      with wt_Ham(phi_n x) != w_H(x) is reported per family.
+  C4  NO map into a Hamming space can be an isometry for the
+      homogeneous weight: w_hom takes the non-integral values
+      1 + 1/(q^2-1) and 1 - 1/((q-1)^2(q+1)) on R = M_2(F_q)
+      (verified exhaustively for q = 4, 8, 9), while Hamming weights
+      are integers.
+  C5  the image of a code is NOT in general a cyclic code: it is
+      quasi-cyclic of index 4t and co-index n, and the number of codes
+      whose image IS invariant under the shift by 1 is reported per
+      family (typically a small minority).
+  C6  phi_n is F_q-linear, NOT R-linear: the target F_q^{4tn} carries
+      no R-module structure; what survives is the transported left
+      regular representation a |-> M_L(a), an injective ring
+      homomorphism R -> M_{4t}(F_q) (checked above).
