+PART 4.  TASK C: EXACT QUANTUM DISTANCE CERTIFICATION
+==============================================================================
+  Every certified code is the EXACT code reported by the search:
+  the search stores the image basis of each code, so no re-selection
+  by invariants takes place.  Three methods are used:
+    M1  complete enumeration of the classical orthogonal code
+        (every codeword; exact and complete when q^dim <= 3*10^6);
+    M2  increasing-weight support search over F_q^N (an independent
+        algorithm: for each support it solves a left-kernel problem);
+    M3  exhaustive search of the AMBIENT quantum space F_q^{2N} in
+        increasing SYMPLECTIC weight, testing commutation with the
+        WHOLE group V (v in V^{perp_omega}; for an EA code the
+        entanglement makes all of V measurable, so an undetected
+        error must commute with V and not merely with rad V) and
+        non-triviality (v not in V).  Complete only up to the weight
+        reached: a return of None proves d > that weight.
+  Report: proved lower bound, proved upper bound (explicit witness),
+  and whether the two coincide.
